# Line endings.
#
# Git on Windows defaults to converting LF to CRLF on checkout. For most files
# that is invisible and harmless. For the files below it is not:
#
#   *.sh        piped to `bash -s` over ssh, a carriage return becomes part of
#               every command, and the shell reports `$'\r': command not found`
#               on a line that looks perfectly correct
#   Dockerfile  the same, inside RUN instructions
#   *.yml       docker compose parses it, but scripts embedded in it break the
#               same way
#   *.sql       psql tolerates it; the diff noise is the problem
#
# Forcing LF on them costs Windows editors nothing — every editor in current use
# handles LF — and removes a class of failure that always presents as something
# other than what it is.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.sql text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf
*.inc text eol=lf
.env.example text eol=lf

# Binary: never touched, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

